1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,533
Shared machines are used by everyone and looked after by no one. COMMONKIT gives each one its own NEAR account.

2
00:00:07,533 --> 00:00:10,767
Open the app. No wallet is needed to look around.

3
00:00:10,767 --> 00:00:15,033
The app: Four shared machines in two communities, read live from NEAR testnet.

4
00:00:15,033 --> 00:00:21,000
The machine: Its account has no keys: funds move through contract rules. The printer itself is simulated.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,033
Book: Pick a time: a small fee, plus a deposit you get back after a clean return.

6
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:30,100
You sign with a NEAR wallet, and the booking is a testnet transaction.

7
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:34,467
Alex's booking on testnet: reservation_confirmed.

8
00:00:34,467 --> 00:00:40,267
Upkeep: At the machine, a bridge unlocks it only for a valid booking and reports usage on chain (simulated).

9
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:44,633
When usage passes a rule, the printer's agent opens an upkeep task. Demo rule: 30 min (real: 200 h).

10
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:48,833
The task: It says why: 4.3 h of nozzle time, over the rule.

11
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:53,800
Ava did the work, the bridge ran a test print, and Mark, another member, approved it.

12
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,933
Earn: Ava earned two usage-right NFTs (NEP-171) for this printer. They cannot be sold or moved.

13
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:02,500
A council member tried to move one. Refused on chain: E_NON_TRANSFERABLE.

14
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,167
Money: Fees stay in the printer's own account, up to a 3 NEAR cap.

15
00:01:06,167 --> 00:01:12,367
Excess goes to the Sputnik DAO. For larger purchases, the machine opens its own proposal.

16
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:19,767
Check it: Every claim can be checked: the Proof page re-reads them from testnet.

17
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:22,600
Or run ./scripts/verify.sh. No wallet, no keys.
